/**
 * German for the Vivir en Espana practice questions.
 *
 * The lessons of this course have read in German since the Spanish table was
 * written; the practice bank behind them had none, so the practice tab and
 * the exam went on asking in Spanish. The fifth of the seven banks.
 *
 * Keyed on the SPANISH of esQuestionBank.ts, exactly as it stands there. Every
 * key was extracted from the built module and paired back by position, never
 * retyped: one wrong character — a missing tilde on an n, an accent dropped —
 * and the lookup misses in silence, so the marker disappears and the reader is
 * told there is nothing for a question that was in fact translated.
 *
 * Names of offices, documents and customs stay Spanish, as they do in
 * VIVIR_EN_ESPANA_DE: Cortes, padron, NIE, concierto economico, tapeo,
 * sobremesa, La Roja. That is what the exam asks for. What is translated is
 * the explanation around them.
 *
 * Strings another German table already answers are deliberately absent. Every
 * table for one target is spread into a single object, so a second entry for
 * the same key would be a silent collision, and the older table would decide
 * the wording for both. check-question-bank-translation counts what a reader
 * reaches rather than what this file holds.
 */
